{
 "clause": "RM-6",
 "document": "15-relaxed-mempool.md",
 "version": 1,
 "also": [
  "RM-3",
  "RM-5"
 ],
 "operation": "pool",
 "distinguishes": "Each block's access list is read for violations of the declared codes: a write to a set declared slot, a second write in one block to an unset one, which the state alone does not show, and a balance drop beyond max_outflow; a first write and a drop within the bound are none. One violation throttles the code at once, ban_violations ban it, and violations decay every declaration_refresh_seconds. A throttled code is relied on by throttled_count relaxed transactions, a banned one by none, and canonical transactions are not counted.",
